Negative control for the EDITOR-IS-THE-MODULE'S-OWN-MUTATE law (`R6-27`).

Falls back to the COLLECTION composable when a module publishes no editor, so a
read-only module still offers its declared handoff controls and the dialog boots
the list in a form's place. The inline spec is what made the handoff stop
pointing at another declaration; this puts back a target that was never
declared.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the playground-shell / handoff binding spec — a declaration with no
`useMutate` binds no handoff at all, so no editor control is offered.

